/* Glucose smoothing algorithm description */
"Glucose is used exactly as the CGM reports it." = "Glucose is used exactly as the CGM reports it.";
"The smoothing used by older iAPS versions, which always ran it with 3 passes. Fits a curve through a window of about 30 minutes around each reading." = "The smoothing used by older iAPS versions, which always ran it with 3 passes. Fits a curve through a window of about 30 minutes around each reading.";
"Tracks glucose and how fast it is changing, along with how sure it is of each. Ignores single readings that disagree with the trend, but follows genuine fast rises and falls." = "Tracks glucose and how fast it is changing, along with how sure it is of each. Ignores single readings that disagree with the trend, but follows genuine fast rises and falls.";
"Each reading is blended into two running averages, a plain one and one that follows the current trend, which counts for 60 percent of the result. The simplest option, and the only one that never revises an earlier reading - so older values on the chart lag behind the raw ones." = "Each reading is blended into two running averages, a plain one and one that follows the current trend, which counts for 60 percent of the result. The simplest option, and the only one that never revises an earlier reading - so older values on the chart lag behind the raw ones.";

/* Glucose smoothing algorithm options description */
"Each extra pass widens the window the curve is fitted over: a little less noise, but sharp peaks and dips are flattened more." = "Each extra pass widens the window the curve is fitted over: a little less noise, but sharp peaks and dips are flattened more.";
"How readily the filter gives up its own trend to follow the readings. Calmer is smoother, but the newest reading lags further behind a sharp turn." = "How readily the filter gives up its own trend to follow the readings. Calmer is smoother, but the newest reading lags further behind a sharp turn.";

